Cons:

* still costs always-on compute
* needs gateway leases
* needs session health UI
* needs channel-specific reconnect behavior

4. Dedicated Hosted Gateway Container

Each paying workspace/user gets a stable persistent container or VPS-backed gateway.

Best for:

* WhatsApp Web/Baileys
* Signal bridge
* browser profiles
* important customers
* higher reliability plans

Pros:

* session stability
* less re-login risk
* stable storage
* stable IP/region possible
* clean isolation

Cons:

* higher cost
* container lifecycle management required
* requires stronger operational monitoring

5. Dedicated Company-Provided Hardware / Workstation

This is the “provided by us” model, similar to a managed Agent Computer.

Best for:

* premium users
* business users
* customers who want always-on automation but do not want to maintain their own machine
* tasks needing more RAM/CPU than tiny VPS

Pros:

* strong product differentiation
* user does not manage hardware
* can support hosted browser / local tools / personal channels

Cons:

* expensive
* security responsibility moves to Empyralis
