Stage 7: Session Persistence Modes

Define these modes clearly.

local_only

For user hardware.

Session files stay only on customer-owned hardware.
Cloud never receives backup blob.
If device dies, user reconnects.

Matches current trust-boundary model best.

gateway_local

For hosted VPS/container MVP.

Session files stay on the hosted gateway persistent volume.
Cloud control plane tracks metadata/status only.
If container restarts with same volume, session survives.
If volume is lost, user reconnects.

Best MVP.

hosted_encrypted_backup

Middle stage.

Session state is encrypted on the hosted gateway and backed up to company storage.
Restore only to same workspace and approved replacement gateway.
Encryption keys are scoped.
Recovery is audited.

cloud_session_vault

Full future version.

Control plane manages encrypted session state blobs and can restore to any trusted gateway host.
Requires stronger key management, vault policy, legal/privacy text, deletion, rotation, export.

Do not start with this unless absolutely needed.

