Stage 9: Worker Wake/Sleep Model

This is the efficiency model.

Heavy workers should sleep.

Gateway should stay alive when required.

Flow:

Incoming message arrives on gateway.
Gateway sends channel.inbound event to control plane.
Control plane records inbound event.
Control plane decides if policy allows automatic reply.
Control plane enqueues agent job.
Worker wakes.
Worker reads thread/memory/context.
Worker drafts or sends response through gateway.
Gateway sends outbound message.
Worker writes result.
Worker sleeps after idle timeout.
Gateway stays alive.

