Stage 12: Security Requirements

This feature is high-risk because personal channel sessions are basically user identity.

Rules:

Never store personal channel secrets in public Studio connector state.
Never display raw tokens/cookies/session files.
Never put session tokens in heartbeat metadata.
Never store raw Telegram/WhatsApp credentials in logs.
Never include raw secrets in diagnostics export.
Never let deployed Studio agents use Sage personal session by default.
Never allow two active gateways to own the same personal channel session.
Never allow workspace mismatch.
Never allow revoked gateway reconnect.
Never let hosted VPS full-access mode claim desktop-only capabilities without bridge.

Encryption:

For MVP gateway-local mode:

File permissions 0600 minimum.
Hosted volume isolated per workspace/gateway.
No shared Chrome/profile/session dir.
Secrets redacted from logs.

For hosted encrypted backup:

Envelope encryption.
Per-workspace data key.
Key reference stored separately from blob.
Blob integrity hash.
Versioned backups.
Explicit deletion flow.
Recovery audit.

