Stage 20: What Happens When User Stops Work

There are different “stop” buttons.

We must distinguish them.

Stop current run

Stops heavy agent worker.
Gateway remains online.
Personal channels remain connected.
Always-on automation may continue depending on policy.

Pause automation

Gateway remains connected.
Inbound messages are recorded.
Agent does not auto-reply.
User can manually resume.

Stop gateway

Gateway disconnects.
Live answering stops.
Session files remain on persistent state.
User can restart gateway later.

Revoke Agent Computer

Gateway trust revoked.
Gateway cannot reconnect.
Personal channel is disconnected from platform.
May optionally delete hosted session state.

Destroy hosted VPS

Live answering stops.
If volume kept, session may restore later.
If volume deleted, session likely lost.

Frontend must not use one vague “Stop” button for all of this. That would be a UI crime scene.

