Final Decision Summary

If only heavy worker stops:

Gateway should stay alive.
Personal channels should stay connected.
Build/verify this.

If gateway process stops:

Live replies stop.
Session should survive if gateway state persists.
Restart should restore.

If VPS/container restarts:

Live replies pause during restart.
Session should survive if persistent volume is mounted.

If VPS/container is destroyed but volume survives:

Session may restore on replacement container using same state.
Need careful gateway identity/recovery handling.

If VPS/container and volume are destroyed:

Session is lost unless encrypted backup/session vault exists.
User reconnects.

If user wants 24/7 replies:

At least one lightweight gateway must remain online.
The heavy agent worker can sleep.

This is the architecture:

Control plane: always on
Hosted/local gateway: durable connector
Heavy worker: temporary compute
Personal session: gateway-local now, encrypted vault later
Memory/audit/policy: central control plane